# Production API variables for Railway (acc-api service).
# Copy values into Railway → acc-api → Variables. Do not commit real secrets.
#
# Railway project layout (production):
#   1. Postgres  — add via Railway "Database" template
#   2. Redis     — add via Railway "Redis" template
#   3. acc-api   — this repo (Dockerfile); set variables below
#
# Postgres and Redis join the project private network automatically.
# On acc-api, use Reference Variables (Variables → Add Reference) so URLs
# stay in sync when Railway rotates credentials.
#
# S3 media remains on AWS ca-central-1 (spec §29).

NODE_ENV=production
HOST=0.0.0.0
# Railway injects PORT automatically — omit unless overriding.

# --- Data stores (Railway: Postgres + Redis services) ---
DATABASE_URL=${{Postgres.DATABASE_URL}}
REDIS_URL=${{Redis.REDIS_URL}}

# --- Auth (generate unique values: openssl rand -hex 32) ---
JWT_ACCESS_SECRET=REPLACE_WITH_64_CHAR_HEX
JWT_REFRESH_SECRET=REPLACE_WITH_DIFFERENT_64_CHAR_HEX
JWT_ACCESS_TTL=15m

# --- HTTP / WebSocket CORS ---
# Comma-separated origins allowed for REST + Socket.IO.
# Include your Railway public API URL (and custom domain if attached).
CORS_ORIGINS=https://acc-api-production.up.railway.app

# --- Public API base URL ---
# Railway domain or custom domain — must match what mobile/EAS uses.
PUBLIC_API_URL=https://acc-api-production.up.railway.app

# --- AWS S3 (ca-central-1) ---
AWS_S3_BUCKET=acc-media-prod
AWS_REGION=ca-central-1
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=REPLACE_WITH_IAM_ACCESS_KEY
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=REPLACE_WITH_IAM_SECRET_KEY
# Do not set AWS_S3_ENDPOINT in production (MinIO dev only).

# --- Phased rollout: stub integrations you don't have yet ---
# Comma-separated list of integrations allowed to run with console stubs in
# production (OTPs / push are LOGGED, not delivered). Remove each entry once you
# add its real credentials below. AWS S3 and CORS cannot be stubbed.
# Leave unset to require all integrations.
ALLOW_STUBBED_INTEGRATIONS=TWILIO,FCM

# --- Twilio SMS (Canadian +1 sender) ---
# Required unless TWILIO is listed in ALLOW_STUBBED_INTEGRATIONS.
# TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=ACxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=REPLACE_WITH_AUTH_TOKEN
# TWILIO_FROM_NUMBER=+1xxxxxxxxxx

# --- Firebase Cloud Messaging ---
# Required unless FCM is listed in ALLOW_STUBBED_INTEGRATIONS.
# FCM_PROJECT_ID=your-firebase-project-id
# FCM_CLIENT_EMAIL=firebase-adminsdk-xxxxx@your-project.iam.gserviceaccount.com
# Paste the service-account private_key with literal \n escapes; wrap in double quotes.
# FCM_PRIVATE_KEY="-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\nREPLACE\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----\n"
# Optional — defaults to com.atmiya.acc.
# IOS_BUNDLE_ID=com.atmiya.acc
# Leave unset/false for TestFlight + App Store (production APNs).
# FCM_APNS_SANDBOX=false

# --- Optional ---
# LOG_LEVEL=warn
# GOOGLE_PLACES_KEY=AIzaSy...
